course: dictionary
lesson: 4268
title: Gravitational: about the force of gravity
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Gravitational is an adjective, a describing word. It means about gravity, the force that pulls things towards each other, like a dropped ball falling to the ground.
explain: Look at the word's parts. It grows from the word gravity, and its ending makes it describe something. So when you see gravitational, ask: what is this about? The answer is always gravity.
explain: Scientists use phrases like «gravitational pull», «gravitational force» and «gravitational field». The word after gravitational (pull, force or field) tells you what is being described, and the word gravitational tells you the topic is gravity.
explain: Read the sentence: «In 2015 the LIGO detectors in the USA first caught gravitational waves, ripples in space from two black holes merging about 1.3 billion light years away.» The word waves tells you what kind of thing it is, and the word gravitational tells you the ripples come from gravity. Swap test: «ripples caused by gravity» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Gravitational means about gravity.
fact: Gravity is the force that pulls things towards each other.
fact: Gravitational is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as «pull», «force» or «waves».
fact: «Gravitational waves» are ripples in space, first caught in 2015 by the LIGO detectors in the USA.
fact: In science, the word describes the pull of planets, stars and the Moon.
exercise: What does gravitational mean? | About the colours of the rainbow | About music played loudly | *About gravity, the force that pulls things towards each other | About cooking, with hot stoves
exercise: In the phrase «gravitational waves», which word tells us the kind of waves? | *gravitational | waves | space | ripples
exercise: Which phrase is about the force of gravity? | a sunny day | a loud drum | a sweet cake | *a gravitational force
test: A scientist writes «the gravitational field around the star». What does gravitational tell us about the field? | It is about the colour of the star | *It is about gravity | It is about water | It is about music
test: What is a good swap for «gravitational pull» to check the meaning? | the pull of a bicycle bell | a loud noise | the pull of a sweet song | *the pull caused by gravity
exam: In 2015 scientists first caught «gravitational waves». What were these waves? | *Ripples in space | Radio songs from the Moon | Ripples in a swimming pool | Lights from a birthday cake
